<mxfile host="app.diagrams.net">
  <diagram name="System Context" id="context">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1700" dy="1000" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1700" pageHeight="1100" background="#ffffff">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        
        <!-- Title -->
        <mxCell id="title" value="E-COMMERCE PLATFORM (Amazon/Flipkart) — System Context" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontSize=22;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#1a237e" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="10" width="1660" height="35" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <mxCell id="subtitle" value="Inventory Consistency + Distributed Locks + CDC Search Sync + Event-Driven Architecture + Strong ACID for Checkout" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=#e8eaf6;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=1;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="150" y="50" width="1400" height="25" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <!-- System Boundary -->
        <mxCell id="system-boundary" value="" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#ff6f00;strokeWidth=4;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="300" y="120" width="1100" height="850" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <mxCell id="system-label" value="E-COMMERCE PLATFORM (Amazon/Flipkart)" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=#ff6f00;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=1;fontSize=16;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#ffffff" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="310" y="130" width="380" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <!-- Core Services Inside System -->
        <mxCell id="services-box" value="MICROSERVICES" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#c8e6c9;strokeColor=#388e3c;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="320" y="180" width="520" height="280" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <mxCell id="service-list" value="• User Service (registration, authentication, profile)&#xa;• Product Service (catalog, CRUD, MongoDB flexible schema)&#xa;• Search Service (Elasticsearch full-text, faceted filters)&#xa;• Cart Service (add/remove items, cross-device sync)&#xa;• Checkout Service (orchestrator: lock → reserve → payment)&#xa;• Inventory Service (qty + reserved_qty pattern, ACID)&#xa;• Order Service (status tracking, lifecycle management)&#xa;• Payment Service (webhook handler, idempotency check)&#xa;• Notification Service (email/SMS on order events)&#xa;• Warehouse Service (pick, pack, ship workflow)&#xa;• Review/Rating Service (product reviews, aggregations)&#xa;• Recommendation Service (ML-based, user purchase history)" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontSize=10;fontFamily=Courier New" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="330" y="210" width="500" height="240" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <!-- Data Stores -->
        <mxCell id="data-stores-box" value="DATA STORES &amp; INFRASTRUCTURE" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e1bee7;strokeColor=#8e24aa;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="860" y="180" width="520" height="280" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <mxCell id="data-stores-list" value="• MongoDB (Product catalog — flexible schema for categories)&#xa;  100M products × 5KB = 500GB, sharded by category&#xa;&#xa;• PostgreSQL (Inventory — qty + reserved_qty, ACID locks)&#xa;  SELECT FOR UPDATE during checkout (row-level locking)&#xa;  Prevents overselling, strong consistency required&#xa;&#xa;• PostgreSQL (Cart — cross-device sync, ACID upserts)&#xa;  ON CONFLICT for concurrent add-to-cart&#xa;&#xa;• MySQL (Orders — ACID transactions, partitioned by month)&#xa;  Order lifecycle, payment references, shipping details&#xa;&#xa;• Elasticsearch (Search — full-text, fuzzy, faceted filters)&#xa;  Synced from MongoDB via CDC (oplog → Kafka → ES indexer)&#xa;  100K searches/sec during sales events&#xa;&#xa;• Redis (Cache + Distributed Locks)&#xa;  SETNX lock:inventory:{product_id} EX 30 (thundering herd)&#xa;  Cache: product, search results, cart (HSET)&#xa;&#xa;• Kafka (Event streaming — order.created, payment.success)&#xa;  Decouples post-checkout workflow (warehouse, notifications)&#xa;&#xa;• S3 + CloudFront (Product images — 500TB, CDN for fast delivery)" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontSize=9;fontFamily=Courier New" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="870" y="210" width="500" height="240" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <!-- Key Design Principles -->
        <mxCell id="principles-box" value="KEY DESIGN PRINCIPLES" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff3e0;strokeColor=#e65100;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="320" y="480" width="1060" height="200" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <mxCell id="principles-list" value="1. INVENTORY CONSISTENCY: Strong ACID required (no overselling). Redis distributed lock (SETNX) prevents&#xa;   thundering herd. PostgreSQL SELECT FOR UPDATE during reservation. reserved_qty column holds stock during&#xa;   checkout→payment window. Actual deduction ONLY after payment.success webhook.&#xa;&#xa;2. CDC FOR SEARCH SYNC: Product Service writes only to MongoDB. CDC pipeline (oplog → Kafka → ES indexer)&#xa;   keeps Elasticsearch fresh within 1-2 sec. No dual-writes, eventual consistency acceptable for search.&#xa;&#xa;3. FLEXIBLE PRODUCT SCHEMA: MongoDB handles different product categories (mobiles have RAM/storage, books&#xa;   have author/ISBN, clothing has size/color) without sparse NULL columns or ALTER TABLE for new categories.&#xa;&#xa;4. TWO-LAYER LOCKING: Layer 1 (Redis SETNX): Fast rejection &lt;1ms, prevents 10K concurrent users hitting DB.&#xa;   Layer 2 (PostgreSQL FOR UPDATE): ACID row lock during inventory read/reserve (500ms). Auto-expires if crash.&#xa;&#xa;5. IDEMPOTENT PAYMENT WEBHOOK: order_id as idempotency key to payment gateway. UNIQUE constraint on&#xa;   payments(order_id) prevents double-charge. Webhook signature validation (HMAC) prevents forgery.&#xa;&#xa;6. EVENT-DRIVEN POST-CHECKOUT: Kafka decouples all work after payment (warehouse pick, email, analytics).&#xa;   Each consumer scales independently, fails independently. 7-day retention enables replay.&#xa;&#xa;7. CART CROSS-DEVICE SYNC: Cart tied to user_id (not session). PostgreSQL source of truth, Redis cache (HSET)&#xa;   for fast reads. Survives cache eviction, syncs across mobile/web/tablet." style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontSize=9;fontFamily=Courier New" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="330" y="510" width="1040" height="160" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <!-- Critical Challenges -->
        <mxCell id="challenges-box" value="🔥 CRITICAL TECHNICAL CHALLENGES" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffebee;strokeColor=#c62828;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="320" y="700" width="1060" height="250" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <mxCell id="challenges-list" value="1. OVERSELLING PREVENTION: Flash sale, 1 unit left, 10K concurrent checkouts. Without locking:&#xa;   all 10K read qty=1 (sufficient), all reserve, 9999 oversold. Solution: Redis SETNX (fast reject 9999)&#xa;   + PostgreSQL FOR UPDATE (serialize the 1 winner's reservation).&#xa;&#xa;2. INVENTORY LOCK DEADLOCK: User starts checkout, network fails, lock held forever. Solution: Redis lock&#xa;   auto-expires (EX 30 sec). PostgreSQL row lock released on transaction COMMIT/ROLLBACK. Idempotent retry safe.&#xa;&#xa;3. PAYMENT WEBHOOK REPLAY: Payment gateway retries webhook on timeout. Without idempotency: inventory&#xa;   deducted twice for same payment. Solution: UNIQUE constraint on payments(order_id), SELECT before INSERT.&#xa;&#xa;4. CART RACE CONDITION: User adds same product from mobile and web simultaneously. Without ON CONFLICT:&#xa;   two cart_items rows for same product_id. Solution: composite UNIQUE (cart_id, product_id) + ON CONFLICT UPDATE.&#xa;&#xa;5. SEARCH STALENESS AT SCALE: 100M products, update propagation to ES. CDC lag spikes to 10 sec during bulk&#xa;   imports. Acceptable: search shows recently-sold-out item briefly → checkout validates inventory anyway.&#xa;&#xa;6. THUNDERING HERD ON DB: 10K users hit checkout simultaneously. PostgreSQL connection pool (200 conns)&#xa;   exhausted in 50ms, all fail. Solution: Redis distributed lock as early rejection before DB touched.&#xa;&#xa;7. PAYMENT FAILURE RECOVERY: Payment succeeds at gateway but webhook delivery fails (network error).&#xa;   Inventory stays reserved forever → stock leak. Solution: Cron job finds orders PENDING_PAYMENT &gt;30min,&#xa;   polls payment gateway status API, reconciles.&#xa;&#xa;8. CROSS-DEVICE CART SYNC LAG: User adds item on mobile, immediately opens web, sees old cart. Solution:&#xa;   Cache-aside pattern — write to PostgreSQL first, invalidate Redis cache, next read rebuilds from DB." style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontSize=8;fontFamily=Courier New" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="330" y="730" width="1040" height="210" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
